---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT, sites } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Contact Tidy Magpie"
  description="How to report a mistake on a Tidy Magpie site or ask a question, and what to include so it can be fixed quickly."
  path="/contact/"
>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="lede">The most useful message is a correction. If something on one of the sites is wrong, we want to know.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Report a mistake or ask a question</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>
      <p>It helps to include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>which site and which page;</li>
        <li>what is wrong, or what you expected to see;</li>
        <li>a link to a source, if you have one.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A correction is checked against its source. If it holds up, it is fixed in the site's data and noted in the
        update log on that site's Sources page. Not every message gets a personal reply.
      </p>

      <h2>Which site is it about?</h2>
      <ul>
        {sites.map((s) => (
          <li><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>For how facts are sourced and checked in the first place, see <a href="/how-we-work/">How we work</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
